--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PREDECESSOR REUSE (no duplicate domain types — DRY)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The module already ships the sibling parity unit `UserImpersonateButton`
(apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/UserImpersonateButton.*) which OWNS the public
impersonation status type `ImpersonationStatus` (struct: `mode: .open|.restricted` +
`activeSubject: String?`) and `ImpersonationMode`. The page REUSES that module-shared
`ImpersonationStatus` rather than declaring a parallel type (a first draft that declared
its own `enum ImpersonationStatus` was caught by the full xcodebuild as
"'ImpersonationStatus' is ambiguous for type lookup" and corrected — see GATE below).
The web discriminated union maps onto the struct: web `open` → `mode == .open`;
web `active` → `activeSubject != nil`; web `inactive` → `mode == .restricted, activeSubject == nil`.
The web-named helpers `isImpersonationOpenMode` / `isImpersonationActive` and the web hook
names `useImpersonationStatus` / `useImpersonationCandidates` are preserved at the Swift
call sites. All other page types (`ImpersonationCandidate`, `ImpersonationCandidatesResponse`,
`ImpersonationDataSource`, `UsersPageState`, `UsersPageModel`) are unique in the module
(verified by grep — no collisions).

