DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI UsersPage (admin Subjects / impersonation) shipped at parity with
the web source: a pure @Observable state holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) exposing
loading / open-mode / empty / error / success over an injectable ImpersonationDataSource seam
(default = a local sample so the populated state renders out of the box, matching the sibling
admin pages); the single GlassPanel reproduces every web branch (open-mode notice, candidates
spinner, retryable error, no-other-subjects empty state, and the subject list whose rows pair the
opaque proxy subject with an Impersonate button disabled while a session is active). Built on the
P2 tokens + P3 shared components (TSGlassPanel/TSEmptyState/TSErrorDisplay/TSSpinner/TSButton/
typography) — no hand-rolled chrome; every visible string from Localizable.xcstrings with web key
names + verbatim English defaults; VoiceOver labels/identifiers on the panel, list, and rows;
adaptive across macOS/iPad/iPhone; deep-linkable via the new .users route (/users + /admin/users
alias) and hosted through the shell's route registry. It REUSES the module-shared ImpersonationStatus
struct (DRY) rather than duplicating it. Verified on BOTH idioms by isolated Swift 6 strict-concurrency
type-checks (0/0, incl. the real shared struct) and an executed model harness (18/18). The full
